  "chunk": "generated text games, though most approaches rely on fine-tuning rather than\n3\nzero-shot reasoning. Ammanabrolu and Riedl [1] demonstrated that incorpo-\nrating commonsense knowledge graphs improves agent performance, suggesting\nthat pure language models lack sufficient world knowledge. More recently, re-\nsearchers have shown that while state-of-the-art LLMs can play some text-based\ngames effectively, they struggle with games requiring long-term planning and\nspatial reasoning [35]—precisely the capabilities central toZork.\n2.1 Reasoning in LLMs\nWith respect to the general reasoning capabilities of LLMs, recent research\nhas investigated various prompting and reasoning frameworks to enhance LLM\nproblem-solving. Wei et al. [34] introduced Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompt-\ning, showing that encouraging step-by-step reasoning improves performance on\narithmetic and commonsense reasoning tasks. Yao et al. [36] extended this with",
